From: Alexander Gurov <aliogu23@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:11:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] SystemUI: Draw the screen corners as a hardware RC mask

With ro.sf.screen_decor_mask, report a synthetic RGBA_8888 MASK display
decoration support, so ScreenDecorHwcLayer draws the corners for the
display engine's rounded-corner block, which SurfaceFlinger marks
through IDisplayConfig.

The RC block takes a linear, untransformed, top-most mask, and software
rendering isn't pre-rotated, so a landscape mask was rejected. Draw it
on the CPU into an ImageReader (CPU_WRITE | COMPOSER_OVERLAY |
GPU_SAMPLED, linear) child surface in the display's native orientation,
with the inverse buffer transform of the window's hint. The window
itself stays empty and transparent, so SurfaceFlinger culls it.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HCu2kUrLkzjzZJEZ6mCKqM
